# Linear-first planning

Applies on **local IDE**, **cloud agents**, and **Cursor iOS** — repo rules sync via `skills-taste` install hooks.

Linear MCP (`linear` / `user-linear`) is the system of record. Workspace: https://linear.app/shashank-sn

## Hard rules

- **Never use TodoWrite** or chat-only task lists. Use Linear issues.
- **Never leave work untracked.** Create or find a Linear issue before coding.
- **Never store plans only in chat.** Put acceptance criteria in the issue or child issues.
- **Always resolve the Linear project** from the repo name before creating issues.

## Resolve Linear project

**Project name = GitHub repo name** (basename from `git remote` or folder name).

Examples: `brandeey` → project `brandeey`, `sayaboutus-service-core` → project `sayaboutus-service-core`.

Org/owner is in the project summary (`github.com/{owner}/{repo}`). If unsure, `list_projects` and match by name.

## Session start

1. Resolve repo name from workspace path or `git remote`.
2. **Linear project name = repo name** (exact match).
3. `list_issues` for that project — report in-progress and todo items.
4. If work has no issue ID, search Linear first; create only if none exists.

## During work

| Event | Linear action |
|-------|---------------|
| Start | **In Progress** |
| Sub-work | Child issues |
| Blocked | Comment + **Blocked** / `blockedBy` |
| PR ready | Comment + **In Review** |
| Shipped | **Done** |

PR/branch names include issue ID (e.g. `SHA-42: fix landing QA`).

## Planning shape

- Small task → one issue + checklist in description
- Feature → parent + child issues per milestone
- Bug → one issue (+ `Bug` label if exists)
- Spike → Todo issue; findings in comments before code
